<Item XName="Eqns" Type="Equation">
<Text>% --------------------------------------------------------------------------&#x000D;&#x000A;% SamplesPerSymbol: Sets the number of sampler per symbol.&#x000D;&#x000A;%                   It MUST be a POSITIVE integer.&#x000D;&#x000A;%&#x000D;&#x000A;% StartUpDelay: Sets the number of startup samples that will be removed.&#x000D;&#x000A;%               It MUST be a POSITIVE integer.&#x000D;&#x000A;%               In addition, it sets the downsampling phase and so it must&#x000D;&#x000A;%               be carefully selected to downsample the input signal at the&#x000D;&#x000A;%               optimal sampling instant.&#x000D;&#x000A;% --------------------------------------------------------------------------&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;% --------------------------------------------------------------------------&#x000D;&#x000A;% ENTER DESIRED GRAPH CHARACTERISTICS HERE&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;SamplesPerSymbol = 8;&#x000D;&#x000A;StartUpDelay = 49;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;% END CHANGES&#x000D;&#x000A;% --------------------------------------------------------------------------&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;% Reset variables to default if they are out of bounds&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;if ( SamplesPerSymbol &lt; 1 )&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x0009;SamplesPerSymbol = 8;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;if ( StartUpDelay &lt; 1 )&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x0009;StartUpDelay = 49;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;using(&apos;Data_Generic_ofdm_w_Interferer&apos;);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;y = RX_Constellation( StartUpDelay:SamplesPerSymbol:end );&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<UnitUse><T>Int</T><D>2</D></UnitUse>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang>
<UsingContext>Data_Generic_ofdm_w_Interferer;</UsingContext></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" /></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Width" Type="Param">
<Data><T>Double</T><D>0.2134556821779044</D></Data></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Notes" UserName="Notes" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial size=5&gt;OFDM - Cognitive Radio collision avoidance &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue ExampleWorkspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Orthogonal frequency-division multiplexing (OFDM) technologies are particularly well suited to Cognitive Radio applications because of the ease with which signals can be adapted to channel conditions and capacity requirements.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;By selectively disabling subcarriers, wideband signals can avoid interfering with narrow-band signals, even if they are located in the same main channel.&amp;nbsp; This example&amp;nbsp;illustrates this concept&amp;nbsp;with the&amp;nbsp;new generic OFDM models.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;An&amp;nbsp;OFDM signal is created&amp;nbsp;with the new generic OFDM models.&amp;nbsp;A narrowband interferer is then summed in with the OFDM signal, along with a cognitive radio spectrum (read from files).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; The narrowband interferer degrades the received constellation and EVM.&amp;nbsp; Reducing the number of subcarriers from 200 (lower center displays)&amp;nbsp;to 160 (lower right&amp;nbsp;displays)&amp;nbsp;and changing the&amp;nbsp;subcarrier allocation&amp;nbsp;enables the OFDM system performance to be improved by avoiding the narrowband interferer.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The number of subcarriers and&amp;nbsp;subcarrier allocation can be changed by clicking on the Equations tab in the schematic window below&amp;nbsp;and changing &quot;CarrierPerOFDMSym&quot; and &quot;CarrierIndex&quot;.&amp;nbsp; CarrierPerOFDMSym defines how many subcarriers are to be used, and CarrierIndex is an array defining the subcarrier allocation.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;For more information on Cognitive Radio, please see&lt;/FONT&gt; &lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0000ff size=2&gt;&lt;FONT color=#0000ff size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;&lt;A href=&quot;http://www.keysight.com/find/eesof-cognitive-whitepaper&quot;&gt;http://www.keysight.com/find/eesof-cognitive-whitepaper&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
